---
/**
 * /privacy-policy/ — linked from the footer on every page, so it must exist
 * and must resolve without an interstitial (Meta's lead ad review fetches it).
 *
 * Indexed: it takes no noindex prop, so it inherits only the sitewide staging
 * flag and becomes indexable at cutover. It is included in the sitemap, since
 * the sitemap filter excludes /thank-you/ and nothing else.
 *
 * Written to describe what this site actually does. Anything not known — data
 * retention, the Conversions API, the analytics stack that is not installed
 * yet — is tracked in PLACEHOLDERS.md rather than invented. There is no
 * postal address here, no DPO, and no claim to any compliance framework the
 * business has not adopted (§2.1 applies to legal text as much as to copy).
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SeamDivider from "../components/SeamDivider.astro";
import { PHONE_DISPLAY, PHONE_HREF, EMAIL, BUSINESS_NAME } from "../data/site";

const EFFECTIVE = "August 29, 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Enviro-Tech Idaho"
  description="What Enviro-Tech Idaho collects when you request an inspection, why we collect it, who it goes to, and how to have it deleted. Plain language."
>
  <section class="container legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal__effective mono">Effective date: {EFFECTIVE}</p>

    <p class="legal__lead">
      This describes what {BUSINESS_NAME} collects through this website, why,
      who it goes to, and how to have it deleted. It is written to be read
      rather than to be impressive. If something here is unclear, call
      <a href={PHONE_HREF}>{PHONE_DISPLAY}</a> and ask.
    </p>

    <SeamDivider />

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      When you submit one of the inspection request forms on this site, you
      give us your name and phone number, which are required, and optionally
      your email address, the city the property is in, the type of problem, and
      whatever you write in the details box. We also record which page the form
      was submitted from, so we know what you were reading when you decided to
      get in touch.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our form handler receives your IP address as part of the request, as any
      web server does. It is used only to limit how many submissions can come
      from one place in a short window, and it is converted to a one-way hash
      before that check runs. We do not store your IP address and we do not
      send it anywhere.
    </p>
    <p>
      Separately, analytics and advertising tools collect information
      automatically as you browse: IP address, device and browser type, and
      which pages you viewed. Those are described below.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>
      To call you back, schedule an inspection, and write you an estimate. That
      is the whole purpose. We use what you tell us about the property to send
      someone who knows what they are walking into, and we use the page you
      submitted from for the same reason.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not add you to a mailing list you did not ask for, and we do not
      text-blast the number you gave us.
    </p>

    <h2>Who it goes to</h2>
    <p>These are the services involved in running this site and handling what you send:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this website and processes form
        submissions. Your request passes through their network.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Make</strong> receives the form submission from our handler and
        routes it to us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager</strong> collect
        analytics about how the site is used.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Meta Pixel and the Meta Conversions API</strong> measure
        advertising performance, including whether an ad led to an inspection
        request.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Each of those handles data under its own terms. We share what the service
      needs to do its job and nothing beyond that.
    </p>

    <h2>Independent testing companies</h2>
    <p>
      This matters more here than on most sites, because of how the work is
      structured. We do not perform laboratory testing. It is done by
      independent testing companies, and that separation is deliberate — the
      company paid to remove a problem should not be the company deciding
      whether you have one.
    </p>
    <p>
      For diagnostic testing, you engage and pay the testing company directly.
      We are not part of that transaction, and we do not pass your information
      to them to set it up. If we give you a name, you contact them yourself.
    </p>
    <p>
      For clearance testing at the end of a job, we engage the testing company
      on your behalf as part of the work. In that case we do share what they
      need to attend and to issue a result: the property address, and a contact
      name and phone number for site access. If you would rather engage the
      clearance testing company yourself, say so and we will arrange it that
      way.
    </p>

    <h2>We do not sell your information</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal information, and we do not trade or rent it. We
      also take no referral fee from the testing companies we may point you
      toward, which is the only reason that recommendation is worth anything.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting your information</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> and ask us to delete what
      you submitted, and we will. You do not need to give a reason or use
      particular wording. If you would rather do it by phone, call
      <a href={PHONE_HREF}>{PHONE_DISPLAY}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      One limit worth stating plainly: if we have already done work for you,
      records tied to that job — the scope, photographs, invoices, and any
      laboratory results — are part of the job file and we keep those. That is
      the documentation a future buyer, an insurer, or you may need later.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
    <p>
      The analytics and advertising tools listed above set cookies and use
      similar technologies to recognize a browser across pages and visits. The
      site itself does not set cookies to run the forms.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings, and every major
      browser allows it. Doing so does not stop you using this site or
      submitting a form. You can also opt out of Google Analytics through
      Google's browser add-on, and adjust advertising preferences in your
      Meta account settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly
      collect information from them. If you believe a child has submitted
      information through this site, email
      <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the effective date at the top changes with it and
      the current version is always the one published here. Where a change
      materially affects what we collect or who it goes to, we will say so on
      this page rather than quietly revising it.
    </p>

    <SeamDivider />

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {BUSINESS_NAME}<br />
      <a href={PHONE_HREF}>{PHONE_DISPLAY}</a><br />
      <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>
    </p>
    <p class="legal__note">
      We are a service-area business and work from your property rather than a
      storefront, so there is no public address to write to. Email or phone
      reaches us directly.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-9);
    max-width: min(var(--container), 52rem);
  }
  .legal__effective {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 62%, var(--surface));
  }
  .legal__lead {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-5);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .legal h2 {
    margin-block: var(--space-7) var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }
  .legal p + p {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
  }
  .legal ul {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .legal li {
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-5);
    position: relative;
  }
  .legal li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-start: 0;
    inset-block-start: 0.62em;
    width: 8px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--seal);
  }
  .legal__note {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 66%, var(--surface));
  }
</style>
